s LOCATIONS & RESOURCES Art Gallery Box Office Theatres EVENTS & PERFORMANCES Arts & Lectures Forum Series Music Ensembles Performing Arts Season Athletics MEN’S SPORTS Baseball Basketball Cross Country Football Soccer Volleyball WOMEN’S SPORTS Basketball Cross Country Golf Soccer Softball Volleyball Flag Football Bowling RESOURCES & FAN ZONE Rockford Regents Alumni STAY IN TOUCH Alumni Alumni Association Contact Us Alumni Awards Transcript & Diploma Request ENGAGE Catalyst FOPA WRCR Golf Playday Day of Giving Homecoming Weekend Charles M. DeWild Hall Of Fame GIVE BACK Gala Alumni Referral Scholarship The Annual Fund Legacy Giving Ways to Give Campus News Rockford.edu / News Adjunct Instructors of Biology 06/05/2026 12:12 pm Rockford University invites applications for part-time instructors of Biology in the Department of Chemical & Biological Sciences for Fall 2026. We are seeking a qualified instructor to teach the following classes: Upper-level Immunology, the in-person course is currently scheduled for Fall 2026 on MWF 2:00-2:50pm. General Biology Laboratory, the in-person lab is currently scheduled for Fall 2026 on Tuesday afternoons from 1:00-3:50pm. Qualifications Ph.D. or M.S. in Biology or Biochemistry. Preference will be given to those with relevant teaching experience. Interested candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae List of three professional references Copies of all relevant transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hire) Application materials should be emailed to HumanResources@rockford.edu Return to Previous Page ROCKFORD UNIVERSITY 5050 East State Street Rockford IL 61108 815.226.4000 Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map & Directions Virtual Tour - Visit Campus Today Library Majors and Minors my.rockford.edu Online Interactive Academic Catalog Employment Opportunities Lang Wellness Center Compliance and Title IX Emergency Information Give News Event Calendar About Rockford University President’s