rum Series Music Ensembles Performing Arts Season Athletics MEN’S SPORTS Baseball Basketball Cross Country Football Soccer Volleyball WOMEN’S SPORTS Basketball Cross Country Golf Soccer Softball Volleyball Flag Football Bowling RESOURCES & FAN ZONE Rockford Regents Alumni STAY IN TOUCH Alumni Alumni Association Contact Us Alumni Awards Transcript & Diploma Request ENGAGE Catalyst FOPA WRCR Golf Playday Day of Giving Homecoming Weekend Charles M. DeWild Hall Of Fame GIVE BACK Gala Alumni Referral Scholarship The Annual Fund Legacy Giving Ways to Give Campus News Rockford.edu / News Kinesiology Adjunct Instructors 10/27/2025 9:30 am Rockford University Department of Kinesiology is seeking adjunct instructors to join our team in the traditional undergraduate majors, Sport Management, Exercise Science, and Physical Education and/ or the Master of Science in Exercise Physiology and the Master of Arts in Sport Management & Leadership programs. If you are passionate and want to join a team of dedicated faculty, we invite you to apply for Fall 2027. Traditional undergraduate adjuncts will teach 16-week face to face courses, including: Teaching Individual and Dual sports, Secondary Physical Education Methods, Adapted Physical Education. Graduate course adjuncts  will teach 8-week asynchronous online courses including: Physiology of Exercise, Applied Exercise & Sport Nutrition, Exercise Testing & Prescription for Special Populations, Principles of Exercise Testing, Prescription & Health Risk Appraisal, Principles of Strength and Conditioning, Biomechanics, Risk Management, Sport Facilities and Event Management, Social & Digital Marketing in Sports, Sport Finance, Managing & Leading Sport Enterprise, Sport Sponsorship & Retention, Sport Governance & Compliance, Ethical Issues & Leadership in Sports, Global Issues in Sport. Preference will be given to candidates who have teaching experience at the college level. Duties and Responsibilities Develop course curriculum Deliver lectures and lead class discussions in an online format Assign homework and projects to help your students learn the material Offer additional help outside of class Mentoring and preparation for certifications Complete grading and other administrative work in a timely manner Requirements and Qualifications: Doctorate degree in your field (required for Masters teaching, preferred for Undergraduate teaching) Professional experience (depending on the field) Online and Face-to-Face teaching experience (preferred) Strong communication skills Computer proficiency Review of applications will start immediately. Interested candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae List of three professional references Copies of all relevant transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hire) Application materials should be emailed to HumanResources@rockford.edu . Rockford University is a small, private, non-profit institution with a curriculum grounded in the liberal arts and complemented by professional and practical experience. The university campus is located in a park-like setting that is nestled into a small urban environment 75 miles northwest of Chicago. At Rockford University, we are committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive environment that values a well-rounded workforce and community. We welcome candidates who, through their professional experience, contribute to excellence in their work and enhance our institutional mission. Return to Previous Page ROCKFORD UNIVERSITY 5050 East State Street Rockford IL 61108 815.226.4000 Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map & Directions Virtual Tour - Visit Campus Today Library Majors and Minors my.rockford.edu Online Interactive Academic Catalog Employment Opportunities Lang Wellness Center Compliance and Title IX Emergency Information Give News Event Calendar About Rockford University President’s Office Privacy Policy IBHE Feedback Scheduling Services and Rentals Copyright © 2026 Rockford University, all rights reserved"
    }
